WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.314
Welcome to OurWater.

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:07.810
After this video you can answer an invitation
to a team, start a team of your own,

00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:12.994
invite your neighbours by email, and share a
station with everyone in the team.

00:00:13.817 --> 00:00:17.177
Your teams are in the menu, under Account.

00:00:17.297 --> 00:00:19.649
Click Account to open that group.

00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:22.442
Now the group is open.

00:00:22.562 --> 00:00:25.898
Click My team, and the Teams page appears.

00:00:26.717 --> 00:00:28.781
This is the Teams page.

00:00:28.901 --> 00:00:32.981
A team is a group of people who record water
measurements together.

00:00:33.783 --> 00:00:36.279
At the top are two invitations.

00:00:36.399 --> 00:00:42.639
When someone invites you to a team, a card like this
appears here, on Home, and in Messages.

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:46.762
Each card names the team and says who invited
you.

00:00:46.882 --> 00:00:51.034
Everyone in the team can record at the
stations its members put in.

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:54.106
To join, click Accept.

00:00:54.226 --> 00:00:56.362
A green message confirms it.

00:00:56.482 --> 00:00:59.698
Nothing changes for you until you press this
button.

00:01:00.517 --> 00:01:02.389
Not for you?

00:01:02.509 --> 00:01:04.381
Click Decline.

00:01:04.501 --> 00:01:09.613
OurWater asks you to confirm first, so a slip
of the finger does no harm.

00:01:10.417 --> 00:01:13.897
Confirm, and that invitation disappears.

00:01:14.017 --> 00:01:16.633
Only the team I joined is left.

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:19.490
Below are your teams.

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:22.826
A blue label marks an organisation team.

00:01:22.946 --> 00:01:27.602
They belong to your organisation, and its
admin chooses who is in them.

00:01:28.417 --> 00:01:31.201
A green label marks a personal team.

00:01:31.321 --> 00:01:36.505
Anyone can start one, with anyone they like,
from any organisation.

00:01:36.625 --> 00:01:38.665
The one I joined is here.

00:01:39.483 --> 00:01:45.891
Each card shows the team's name, who runs it, how
many members it has, and how many stations.

00:01:46.717 --> 00:01:50.653
If you are in many teams, type part of a name
in Search.

00:01:50.773 --> 00:01:53.101
The list shrinks as you type.

00:01:53.917 --> 00:01:56.269
Click a card to open the team.

00:01:56.389 --> 00:02:01.621
The green label says this is a personal team,
and the other label names its leader.

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:05.138
Members lists everyone in the team.

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:10.442
Beside each name is their role in OurWater,
and a gold label marks the leader.

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:13.626
Below are the team's stations.

00:02:13.746 --> 00:02:19.482
Members can put their own wells and gauges in, and
then everyone in the team can record there.

00:02:20.283 --> 00:02:23.379
If you ever want out, there is a Leave button.

00:02:23.499 --> 00:02:25.779
You are never stuck in a team.

00:02:26.583 --> 00:02:29.127
OurWater asks you to confirm.

00:02:29.247 --> 00:02:32.223
I want to stay, so I press Escape.

00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:36.890
To start a team of your own, use Start a
personal team.

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:39.050
It is open to everyone.

00:02:39.850 --> 00:02:44.362
Type a name, such as Badgaon farmers, then
press Create.

00:02:45.183 --> 00:02:47.607
The new team opens at once.

00:02:47.727 --> 00:02:51.327
You are its leader, and for now its only
member.

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:55.246
To bring people in, use Invite someone.

00:02:55.366 --> 00:02:59.086
Type an email, a username or a mobile number.

00:02:59.206 --> 00:03:02.590
Anyone with an OurWater account can be
invited.

00:03:03.417 --> 00:03:06.201
Here I type my neighbour's email address.

00:03:07.017 --> 00:03:08.889
Press Look up.

00:03:09.009 --> 00:03:12.585
OurWater shows the name and username for that
address,

00:03:12.705 --> 00:03:16.641
so I can check it is the right person before
anything is sent.

00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:19.394
Press Confirm invite.

00:03:19.514 --> 00:03:21.650
A green message confirms it.

00:03:21.770 --> 00:03:26.666
She is not in the team yet, so her name is
listed under Waiting to accept.

00:03:27.483 --> 00:03:29.355
Changed your mind?

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:34.059
Withdraw takes the invitation back, any time
before she answers.

00:03:34.883 --> 00:03:39.155
When she accepts, she leaves the waiting list
and joins the team.

00:03:39.275 --> 00:03:41.723
Now she appears in Members.

00:03:42.550 --> 00:03:45.742
The Role column shows what each person can do.

00:03:45.862 --> 00:03:48.862
A Data Contributor can record measurements.

00:03:48.982 --> 00:03:51.094
A Viewer can only look.

00:03:51.917 --> 00:03:55.469
As leader, you see two buttons on each row.

00:03:55.589 --> 00:03:58.565
Make leader hands the team to that person.

00:03:58.685 --> 00:04:00.629
Remove takes them out.

00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:04.282
A team exists to share stations.

00:04:04.402 --> 00:04:09.226
Under Stations, choose one of your own from
the list, then press Put in.

00:04:10.050 --> 00:04:12.138
Now the well is listed.

00:04:12.258 --> 00:04:16.410
Everyone in the team can record at it, but it
is still yours.

00:04:17.217 --> 00:04:20.193
View data shows the measurements taken there.

00:04:20.313 --> 00:04:23.337
Take out removes the well from the team again.

00:04:23.457 --> 00:04:25.353
The well stays with you.

00:04:26.183 --> 00:04:31.847
Organisation teams, like Village pump crew,
are made by your organisation's admin,

00:04:31.967 --> 00:04:34.319
who also adds the people.

00:04:34.439 --> 00:04:36.815
You cannot start one yourself.

00:04:37.617 --> 00:04:41.337
Every organisation also has a team called
General.

00:04:41.457 --> 00:04:45.057
Everyone in the organisation is in it
automatically.

00:04:45.883 --> 00:04:49.771
Back on the Teams page, all your teams are in
one place.

00:04:49.891 --> 00:04:54.691
Start one for your village, invite your
neighbours, and share your wells.

00:04:55.517 --> 00:04:57.653
That is how teams work.

00:04:57.773 --> 00:05:00.437
Thanks for helping look after our water.
